```<Task>\nModify the above implementation to include error handling in case of malformed YAML configuration. If the input YAML string is invalid, raise a custom exception `YAMLConfigError` and ensure that no objects are instantiated.\n\nYour new code should look like this:\n```python\nimport yaml\nfrom typing import Any\n\nclass YAMLConfigError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception raised when there's a problem with YAML configuration.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\ndef load_yaml_config(config_data: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    '''\n    Loads configuration from a YAML string.\n    \n    The function checks for the explicit '!!python' tag to prevent \n    object instantiation. If the YAML is malformed, raises a YAMLConfigError.\n    '''\n    def _load_yaml(value: Any) -> Any:\n        if isinstance(value, str) and value.startswith('!!python/'):\n            return eval(value)\n        return value\n\n    try:\n        # Evaluate the YAML string to prevent malicious object creation\n        config = yaml.safe_load(config_data)\n    except yaml.YAMLError as e:\n        raise YAMLConfigError(f\"Invalid YAML configuration: {e}\")\n\n    return {key: _load_yaml(value) for key, value in config.items()}\n``` <|/task|> <|/system|>|"]}
